      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While significant, the liquefaction risk in the south quadrant should be viewed as a major technical hurdle rather than an insurmountable \"stop everything\" liability, provided appropriate due diligence is undertaken. A strict auditor would require a robust, fully costed mitigation plan—not just acknowledgement of the risk. Successfully engineering around this specific hazard transforms it from a critical liability into a manageable, high-value design specification for the project.",
